you,

262
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:11,163
and this woman.

263
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:14,500
What is the connection there?

264
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,753
How am I supposed to know?

265
00:22:18,921 --> 00:22:20,840
Why did you try to kill this woman?

266
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:22,675
I don't know.

267
00:22:24,093 --> 00:22:25,553
I honestly don't know anything.

268
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,138
Tell me.

269
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,641
I know you know.

270
00:22:31,392 --> 00:22:32,393
I don't know, man.

271
00:22:33,394 --> 00:22:35,020
I was only doing what I was told.

272
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,565
Oh my! What…

273
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:49,410
Dr. Kang, what are you doing here?

274
00:22:49,952 --> 00:22:52,621
I'm here to check on the patient
I operated on. Are you okay?

275
00:22:53,581 --> 00:22:54,623
Yeah.

276
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:58,168
I was just about to leave.

277
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:00,337
Can you wake him up?

278
00:23:01,964 --> 00:23:04,049
Okay.

279
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:08,178
Isn't it so tense
at the hospital these days?

280
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:09,722
Is it?

281
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:14,142
Well, nobody talks about it,
but everyone thinks it's weird.

282
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:17,729
They're only keeping it quiet
because it's about Ms. Ko and Dr. Kang--

283
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:23,110
Geez.

284
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:25,863
That was Dr. Ha, wasn't it?

285
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:27,781
What's wrong with him?

286
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,409
- Darn it.
- Beats me.

287
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:47,509
KO DONGCHAN, DIRECTOR

288
00:24:38,769 --> 00:24:40,062
Scary, isn't it?

289
00:24:41,939 --> 00:24:43,107
Mom.

290
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:46,443
We took him in as part
of our family, and now this.

291
00:24:58,706 --> 00:25:00,541
How could he do something like that?

292
00:25:05,087 --> 00:25:06,130
How are you feeling?

293
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,092
Maybe you should go back to the hospital.

294
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:12,386
I'm fine, Mom.

295
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:14,513
I just want to rest at home.

296
00:25:15,305 --> 00:25:16,306
Okay.

297
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,310
We should get that fixed soon.

298
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:35,951
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

299
00:25:40,456 --> 00:25:43,000
Mom, I'll finish up here.

300
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,461
You should head home.

301
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,721
Sorry, we're…

302
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:08,525
Taeju.

303
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,236
Hi, Mom.

304
00:26:12,780 --> 00:26:13,863
Where…

305
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:19,578
I'm sorry.

306
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:22,122
Save your apology for later.

307
00:26:25,918 --> 00:26:27,086
It's fine.

308
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:31,048
As long as you're okay.

309
00:26:33,509 --> 00:26:34,926
It's fine.

310
00:26:34,927 --> 00:26:37,471
Man, you look rough.

311
00:26:39,515 --> 00:26:41,517
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

312
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:45,937
What about Seyun? Is she okay too?

313
00:26:45,938 --> 00:26:48,273
Yeah, she's fine. She's safe.

314
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:51,652
Oh, thank goodness.

315
00:26:52,986 --> 00:26:56,365
I'm so relieved.

316
00:27:00,828 --> 00:27:01,995
I see.

317
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:08,127
And so, have you talked to Seyun?

318
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,630
Well, we haven't really had a chance
to talk things through yet.

319
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,049
Why not?

320
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,760
It's just…

321
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:19,262
I don't want any more misunderstandings.

322
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:21,390
Surely, it can't get any worse.

323
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:24,433
You even shot up her parents' house,

324
00:27:24,434 --> 00:27:25,727
- so how could it--
- Taeyeong.

325
00:27:31,567 --> 00:27:33,610
How are you going to set things straight?

326
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:36,405
Just sit down and talk to her.

327
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:40,534
You can't avoid it forever.

328
00:27:42,286 --> 00:27:44,162
Not yet. Well…

329
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:47,666
There are a few things
I need to verify first.

330
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:51,587
I can't really clear the air
with Seyun until I do.

331
00:27:54,006 --> 00:27:55,173
Taeju.

332
00:27:57,634 --> 00:27:58,635
Yes?

333
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:03,891
Look, I don't know the ins and outs
of your marriage,

334
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,185
but don't drag this out.

335
00:28:08,437 --> 00:28:09,980
The longer you let this sit,

336
00:28:10,856 --> 00:28:14,192
the more difficult it will be
to set things straight.

337
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:19,114
And at that point, it'll be too late.

338
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:22,450
Whatever you're going to do,
don't take too long.

339
00:28:22,451 --> 00:28:23,452
You understand?

340
00:28:25,913 --> 00:28:27,080
Yeah.

341
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:41,261
Why don't you stay the night?

342
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:43,722
Okay.

343
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:53,689
- Here.
- Oh, no, I'm good.

344
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:54,900
Let me pour you one.

345
00:29:04,201 --> 00:29:05,202
What's so funny?

346
00:29:07,537 --> 00:29:10,290
You're just so fickle, aren't you?

347
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:13,126
What do you mean?

348
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:18,923
I mean, at first,
you couldn't live without her,

349
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:22,218
and then you couldn't stand
living with her.

350
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:26,180
And now, you're putting
your life on the line to save the woman

351
00:29:26,181 --> 00:29:28,224
you couldn't stand living with.

352
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:31,311
That's pretty fickle, isn't it?

353
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:36,775
Do you know why I wanted
to end things with Seyun?

354
00:29:40,237 --> 00:29:41,238
Why?

355
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:50,956
I didn't want her to be lonely
or in pain anymore.

356
00:29:56,044 --> 00:29:58,671
Why are you getting all deep on me now?

357
00:29:58,672 --> 00:30:00,048
Make it make sense.

358
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:04,302
I thought it was the right thing to do.

359
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:07,347
To let her off the leash.

360
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:14,604
But I think I was wrong.

361
00:30:15,897 --> 00:30:17,524
I'm done running away now.

362
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:23,571
Usually, these types of crimes
are committed by a lone wolf,

363
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:25,948
but in this case,
we're looking at a married couple.

364
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:27,491
MARRIED COUPLE IN ON THE CRIME

365
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:29,035
Isn't that utterly shocking?

366
00:30:29,036 --> 00:30:30,786
It's beyond disturbing.

367
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:32,538
And what's even more shocking?

368
00:30:32,539 --> 00:30:34,041
They barely even know me.

369
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,584
They've never even talked to me,

370
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:38,544
but the second
something like this happens,

371
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:41,464
they all start running their mouths
like they know all about me.

372
00:30:41,465 --> 00:30:43,174
…that he was always kind and polite.

373
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:46,094
And yet, he's accused
of committing these heinous acts.

374
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:51,391
He was a kind teacher by day
but a depraved criminal by night.

375
00:30:51,892 --> 00:30:53,894
He was living an absolute double life.

376
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:57,396
Exactly.
That's what makes it so terrifying.

377
00:30:57,397 --> 00:30:58,481
Don't you think so?

378
00:30:58,482 --> 00:31:01,067
He didn't fit the profile of a criminal.

379
00:31:01,068 --> 00:31:03,820
No sinister looks, no red flags.

380
00:31:10,452 --> 00:31:15,373
JANG BONE-BROTH SUNDAEGUK

381
00:31:16,166 --> 00:31:19,169
- Hello.
-  Hi, how are you?

382
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:23,590
Oh, dear.

383
00:31:26,760 --> 00:31:29,429
You're back again.

384
00:31:30,055 --> 00:31:31,223
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

385
00:31:32,641 --> 00:31:34,391
Oh, hey. You're here.

386
00:31:34,392 --> 00:31:36,393
I wanted to grab a bite
before heading home.

387
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:38,062
Well, I'm glad you came.

388
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:40,941
Oh, right. Ever since you fixed it,

389
00:31:41,650 --> 00:31:44,568
that machine hasn't acted up once.
It's all thanks to you.

390
00:31:44,569 --> 00:31:46,696
Oh, come on, it was nothing.

391
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:48,698
So, one gukbap?

392
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:52,285
- Yeah.
- Okay, give me a moment.

393
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:05,048
-  Detective Oh!
- Yes, sir.

394
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:10,011
FORENSICS

395
00:32:28,655 --> 00:32:29,864
Darn.

396
00:32:41,501 --> 00:32:42,918
What the hell is this?

397
00:32:42,919 --> 00:32:46,256
Wow, this guy is completely nuts.

398
00:33:01,438 --> 00:33:04,481
Collect every luminol-positive bloodstain
in the basement,

399
00:33:04,482 --> 00:33:05,650
and send them to the NFS.

400
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:08,235
Request blood analysis
and DNA comparison too.

401
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:09,237
Yes, sir.

402
00:33:10,238 --> 00:33:12,948
We don't know what else we'll find,
so search every inch.

403
00:33:12,949 --> 00:33:13,950
Yes, sir.

404
00:33:21,374 --> 00:33:22,499
What's that?

405
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:23,501
It's a cell phone.

406
00:33:24,502 --> 00:33:26,003
It was under the fridge.

407
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,464
- The fridge?
- Yeah.

408
00:33:30,342 --> 00:33:32,676
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

409
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:34,763
CLOSED FOR TODAY

410
00:33:52,239 --> 00:33:53,990
Dr. Ha. A moment.

411
00:33:58,370 --> 00:33:59,453
Dr. Kang!

412
00:33:59,454 --> 00:34:02,415
You didn't have to
come down here yourself, sir.

413
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:07,170
I heard Dr. Kang personally verified
the label on the Park Dohyeon case today.

414
00:34:07,837 --> 00:34:11,466
The entire future of this hospital
is riding on this project.

415
00:34:13,677 --> 00:34:14,760
What about the logs?

416
00:34:14,761 --> 00:34:16,971
I've already backdated
the culture logs to match.

417
00:34:16,972 --> 00:34:18,515
What's going on here?

418
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:21,434
Dr. Kang.

419
00:34:25,522 --> 00:34:27,148
What am I looking at?

420
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:31,861
Why are there two stem cell samples
from the same patient?

421
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:34,072
Dr. Ha.

422
00:35:19,576 --> 00:35:20,827
Take a sip.

423
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:26,666
What's going on?

424
00:35:34,257 --> 00:35:36,217
I wish you hadn't found out.

425
00:35:38,678 --> 00:35:42,932
Although I did think
that you would find out someday.

426
00:35:44,434 --> 00:35:47,604
Switching out a patient's
stem cell sample with a fetus's?

427
00:35:50,023 --> 00:35:51,107
Why would you do this?

428
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:54,819
There are limits
to stem cells from an adult.

429
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:57,238
You may be good,

430
00:35:58,156 --> 00:36:01,368
but you were far beneath
the success rate we're aiming for.

431
00:36:03,036 --> 00:36:05,413
However, after we switched them out,

432
00:36:06,206 --> 00:36:07,791
it was a different story.

433
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,461
You did the surgeries, so you should know

434
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:13,922
what we've accomplished.

435
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:18,635
The patients consented to the procedure
thinking it was their own stem cells.

436
00:36:19,386 --> 00:36:21,345
This is completely illegal, Father.

437
00:36:21,346 --> 00:36:23,181
Those illegal procedures

438
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:27,310
helped people regain movement
and stand on their own two feet.

439
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:31,606
What do you make of those results?

440
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:36,027
You've seen them.

441
00:36:36,695 --> 00:36:40,115
The faces they make after the procedure.

442
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,743
Those people had given up,

443
00:36:44,786 --> 00:36:47,580
but now, they're hopeful
and excited about the future.

444
00:36:49,332 --> 00:36:50,333
Couldn't you just

445
00:36:50,834 --> 00:36:54,796
let them have that hope?

446
00:36:57,716 --> 00:36:59,259
That is not hope.

447
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:06,057
Any hope that's built on a lie
is bound to fall apart.

448
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:10,562
Knowingly giving them false hope…

449
00:37:12,981 --> 00:37:14,899
That's not hope. It's deception.

450
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:20,196
Please count me out of this project.

451
00:37:26,953 --> 00:37:28,079
What about Seyun?

452
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:34,419
What will you do about her?

453
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:25,344
Can you check
Ms. Kim Gyeongae's vitals every hour?

454
00:38:25,345 --> 00:38:26,553
Okay, I will.

455
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:27,972
But Dr. Choi.

456
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:31,017
How long will she be at our hospital?

457
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:32,977
Why?

458
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:36,855
I mean, it's just uncomfortable.

459
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:38,398
Everyone feels that way.

460
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:40,610
Well, she's still a patient.
She has to recover.

461
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:48,033
I'm going to head home.
Let me know when she wakes up.

462
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:49,244
Okay.

463
00:39:41,838 --> 00:39:44,006
INCOMING CALL
GRANDDAUGHTER

464
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:52,974
Grandma! Why can't I reach you?

465
00:39:58,021 --> 00:39:59,230
Who are you?

466
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,399
Catch your breath now.

467
00:40:01,983 --> 00:40:02,984
Have a seat.

468
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:09,824
Don't you remember me?

469
00:40:11,993 --> 00:40:14,536
Sweetheart, can you set his table?

470
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:15,538
Okay, Grandma.

471
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:19,667
Your grandmother's told me all about you.

472
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,337
- Nice to meet you.
- Likewise.

473
00:40:22,921 --> 00:40:24,672
You know Woori Together Medical Center?

474
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:27,591
She works as a nurse there.

475
00:40:27,592 --> 00:40:29,052
Ah!

476
00:40:29,636 --> 00:40:30,720
Yeah, I've been there.

477
00:40:31,638 --> 00:40:34,765
She helps me out
whenever she can, after her shift.

478
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:37,851
She's not like
the other young people these days.

479
00:40:37,852 --> 00:40:40,313
That's amazing. You must be proud of her.

480
00:40:41,064 --> 00:40:43,274
What are you doing here?

481
00:40:44,651 --> 00:40:46,235
Where's my grandma?

482
00:40:47,195 --> 00:40:48,279
Your grandma?

483
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:50,281
She's gone on a trip.

484
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:53,618
She was in a hurry,
so she wanted me to watch the place.

485
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:55,828
But that's her phone.

486
00:40:57,163 --> 00:40:59,832
Oh, yeah. She must've forgotten.

487
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:04,837
Where is my grandma?

488
00:41:07,256 --> 00:41:09,216
I said, she's on a trip.

489
00:41:09,217 --> 00:41:12,094
Why would she suddenly go on a trip
without even telling me?

490
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:14,639
Guess she didn't feel like telling you.

491
00:41:15,807 --> 00:41:16,975
Where's my grandma?

492
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:19,226
Where is she?

493
00:41:19,227 --> 00:41:21,728
I'm going to call the cops.

494
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:23,481
If you do, I feel like I might…

495
00:41:26,234 --> 00:41:27,777
forget where your grandma is.

496
00:41:29,946 --> 00:41:30,947
My grandma…

497
00:41:32,448 --> 00:41:33,950
Is she safe?

498
00:41:38,705 --> 00:41:39,998
We'll see.

499
00:41:43,793 --> 00:41:45,211
It depends on how you do.

500
00:41:51,426 --> 00:41:52,969
Anyway, that being said…

501
00:41:54,012 --> 00:41:55,971
I want you to get rid of my wife.

502
00:41:55,972 --> 00:41:57,890
What? What did you say?

503
00:41:58,558 --> 00:41:59,976
Get rid of my wife.

504
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:02,228
Ms. Ko.

505
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:06,024
How does that make you feel?

506
00:42:07,442 --> 00:42:08,609
I know this is fake.

507
00:42:10,069 --> 00:42:12,196
There's no way he said anything like that.

508
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:14,490
I know you don't want to believe it.

509
00:42:14,991 --> 00:42:16,324
But hey.

510
00:42:16,325 --> 00:42:22,248
You already know
that your husband doesn't love you.

511
00:42:33,509 --> 00:42:34,594
No!

512
00:42:37,388 --> 00:42:40,891
That video. It's all a misunderstanding.

513
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:42,517
I can explain all of it.

514
00:42:42,518 --> 00:42:44,187
I'm telling you the truth.

515
00:42:44,854 --> 00:42:47,356
Please. Please just believe me.

516
00:42:48,024 --> 00:42:49,858
Seyun.

517
00:42:49,859 --> 00:42:51,443
Seyun, come on.

518
00:42:51,444 --> 00:42:54,196
Seyun. Come on. Please.

519
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:55,405
Seyun.

520
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:57,240
Seyun, can you hear me?

521
00:42:57,241 --> 00:42:58,826
Hey, are you okay?

522
00:43:09,212 --> 00:43:10,630
What did you say?

523
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:12,381
What?

524
00:43:13,341 --> 00:43:15,093
What are you saying?

525
00:43:15,593 --> 00:43:17,427
Ugh. Calm down.

526
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:19,138
I can't understand a word!

527
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:21,599
What?

528
00:43:22,391 --> 00:43:24,185
Kang Taeju was there?

529
00:43:24,977 --> 00:43:26,479
Why are you telling me this now?

530
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:29,231
You know what a huge problem
you've caused?

531
00:43:29,232 --> 00:43:30,857
Where are you right now?

532
00:43:30,858 --> 00:43:33,694
I'll take care of it myself.
Just come to the hospital.

533
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:36,279
No.

534
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:39,367
Just come back to the hospital!

535
00:44:13,609 --> 00:44:15,069
Taeju?

536
00:44:29,876 --> 00:44:31,127
What about Seyun?

537
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:33,337
What will you do about her?

538
00:44:34,130 --> 00:44:36,591
What if the whole world finds out?

539
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:39,218
A father who's a criminal,

540
00:44:40,136 --> 00:44:44,307
the hospital that turned a blind eye,
and the husband at the center of it all.

541
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:49,312
Seyun will have to shoulder all of that.

542
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:53,649
Whether you do the surgery or not,
that's your call.

543
00:44:55,276 --> 00:44:59,697
But it won't be you who pays the price.

544
00:45:00,740 --> 00:45:02,241
It will be Seyun.

545
00:45:04,994 --> 00:45:08,998
What her life will be like after that…

546
00:45:11,292 --> 00:45:12,877
Have you thought about that?

547
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,733
I'm here to check on her.

548
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:19,485
Okay.

549
00:47:04,280 --> 00:47:05,281
It's me.

550
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:09,785
Her BP and heart rate seem normal,
and her breathing's stable.

551
00:47:10,911 --> 00:47:14,165
She's not conscious yet,
but she seems stable.

552
00:47:17,126 --> 00:47:18,419
Keep an eye on her.

553
00:47:18,919 --> 00:47:19,920
Okay.

554
00:47:20,421 --> 00:47:22,882
Oh, and one more thing.

555
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:27,303
Dr. Kang stopped by her room yesterday.

556
00:47:28,137 --> 00:47:29,472
What are you…

557
00:47:30,848 --> 00:47:32,766
I thought he was arrested.

558
00:47:32,767 --> 00:47:34,602
I'm not sure what happened either.

559
00:47:35,144 --> 00:47:37,313
I talked to another nurse,

560
00:47:38,147 --> 00:47:41,776
and it seems he snuck in
while the police officer was asleep.

561
00:47:45,821 --> 00:47:47,073
Tell me all the details.

562
00:47:48,157 --> 00:47:50,743
Apparently, he said he came
to check on the patient

563
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:53,579
and then just left.

564
00:48:10,096 --> 00:48:12,514
NEUROSURGERY
HA JEONGSOO

565
00:48:16,143 --> 00:48:18,520
INCOMING CALL
ILSEUNG CAPITAL

566
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:31,909
CAPTAIN, MAJOR CRIMES UNIT 1
LIEUT. JANG DOSIK

567
00:48:32,910 --> 00:48:34,035
Captain.

568
00:48:34,036 --> 00:48:35,037
Yeah?

569
00:48:35,538 --> 00:48:36,704
You should see this.

570
00:48:36,705 --> 00:48:39,082
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

571
00:48:39,083 --> 00:48:40,084
"To the hospital?"

572
00:48:40,751 --> 00:48:43,212
- Is that all?
- Yeah, everything else was wiped clean.

573
00:48:44,797 --> 00:48:47,507
Get Kim Gyeongae's phone
to Forensics now.

574
00:48:47,508 --> 00:48:49,802
- We have to recover all of it.
- On it, sir.

575
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:57,476
She's been in touch
with someone in the hospital.

576
00:49:08,529 --> 00:49:12,032
PAY BACK BY MORNING,
OR WE'LL SEE YOU AT YOUR GIRL'S PRESCHOOL

577
00:49:15,786 --> 00:49:17,288
Darn, Kang Taeju.

578
00:49:18,330 --> 00:49:20,166
If only he hadn't shown up.

579
00:49:30,843 --> 00:49:31,844
Dr. Ha!

580
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:34,805
Oh, hi.

581
00:49:41,020 --> 00:49:42,605
Working late tonight, Dr. Ha?

582
00:49:44,064 --> 00:49:45,065
Uh, yeah.

583
00:49:45,691 --> 00:49:46,692
Me too.

584
00:50:20,476 --> 00:50:22,728
Dr. Ha!

585
00:50:25,856 --> 00:50:27,066
How did this happen?

586
00:50:28,108 --> 00:50:29,527
I told you to be cautious!

587
00:50:30,069 --> 00:50:31,403
Dr. Ko?

588
00:50:38,661 --> 00:50:40,204
What the hell are you doing here?

589
00:50:41,622 --> 00:50:45,125
I could ask you the same thing.
What are you doing here so late?

590
00:50:46,335 --> 00:50:48,087
Oh, let me guess.

591
00:50:49,922 --> 00:50:53,509
You're not here to see Dr. Ha, are you?

592
00:50:54,176 --> 00:50:56,595
I'm the one asking questions.

593
00:50:57,930 --> 00:50:59,431
What are you doing here?

594
00:51:00,015 --> 00:51:01,642
I just had to check something.

595
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:03,644
"Check something"?

596
00:51:05,020 --> 00:51:07,940
Yeah, it turns out
that woman, Kim Gyeongae,

597
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:10,401
was one of our patients.

598
00:51:11,694 --> 00:51:13,946
And Dr. Ha was her attending physician.

599
00:51:16,991 --> 00:51:18,492
Were you aware of that?

600
00:51:22,121 --> 00:51:23,122
So?

601
00:51:24,832 --> 00:51:26,000
What are you getting at?

602
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:30,838
I caught him right before he injected
potassium chloride into her IV.

603
00:51:31,547 --> 00:51:33,173
I barely stopped him.

604
00:51:34,883 --> 00:51:36,176
What possible reason

605
00:51:37,303 --> 00:51:41,473
could he have
to do such a thing to that woman?

606
00:51:46,687 --> 00:51:49,273
That's what I wanted to know.

607
00:51:50,024 --> 00:51:55,529
But she's unconscious,
and I have no clue where Dr. Ha is.

608
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:58,282
So I'm out of options.

609
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:02,119
Considering you're the hospital director,

610
00:52:03,370 --> 00:52:05,456
I thought you might know a thing or two.

611
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:15,466
One of our patients…

612
00:52:16,175 --> 00:52:17,718
Dr. Ha's patient

613
00:52:19,303 --> 00:52:21,180
was one of Seyun's kidnappers.

614
00:52:22,806 --> 00:52:24,391
Why on earth did she do that?

615
00:52:28,395 --> 00:52:31,231
You should ask that
to that criminal of a woman.

616
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:35,069
Why are you asking me?

617
00:52:36,528 --> 00:52:39,698
Sure, but don't you think
it's a bit weird?

618
00:52:40,616 --> 00:52:41,950
That woman

619
00:52:43,452 --> 00:52:46,622
seems to know so much about you.

620
00:52:51,251 --> 00:52:53,796
You've known Kim Gyeongae
all along, haven't you?

621
00:52:54,546 --> 00:52:57,424
After what you did to my wife…

622
00:52:58,884 --> 00:53:01,136
Maybe you're not worth saving.

623
00:53:07,226 --> 00:53:11,480
I could say the same thing
about that father-in-law of yours.

624
00:53:12,189 --> 00:53:18,237
That scumbag extending his own lifespan
by using those unborn babies.

625
00:53:20,739 --> 00:53:24,743
She knew that you were using
stem cells from fetuses.

626
00:53:25,703 --> 00:53:27,579
She knew all the details.

627
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:35,254
Isn't that why you tried to shut her up…

628
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:39,258
with the help of Dr. Ha?

629
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:42,468
Why did you try to kill this woman?

630
00:53:42,469 --> 00:53:44,179
I don't know.

631
00:53:45,097 --> 00:53:46,724
I honestly don't know anything.

632
00:53:47,516 --> 00:53:48,850
I know you know.

633
00:53:48,851 --> 00:53:50,060
I don't know, man.

634
00:53:50,894 --> 00:53:53,397
I was only doing as I was told. Okay?

635
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:57,151
You and Kim Gyeongae.

636
00:53:59,445 --> 00:54:01,155
What is the connection between you two?

637
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:06,952
The woman who knows the secret
behind the project

638
00:54:08,203 --> 00:54:10,080
kidnapped my wife.

639
00:54:10,998 --> 00:54:12,624
Is that really a coincidence?

640
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:14,585
So what?

641
00:54:16,837 --> 00:54:18,380
Are you suggesting

642
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:22,217
that I had my own daughter kidnapped?

643
00:54:23,343 --> 00:54:24,470
Did you not?

644
00:54:25,345 --> 00:54:26,680
You've lost your mind.

645
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:29,683
Well…

646
00:54:30,893 --> 00:54:32,394
Do you have any evidence?

647
00:54:35,063 --> 00:54:36,356
You don't, do you?

648
00:54:38,484 --> 00:54:40,235
If you want to know so badly,

649
00:54:42,446 --> 00:54:45,532
ask that woman once she wakes up.

650
00:54:47,159 --> 00:54:48,368
Either that

651
00:54:49,912 --> 00:54:53,081
or ask Ha Jeongsoo,
wherever the hell he is.

652
00:55:28,200 --> 00:55:29,660
CALLING
NS_HA JEONGSOO

653
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:54,977
PARKING

654
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:10,409
WING B, B3F

655
00:57:47,255 --> 00:57:50,258
DIRECTOR KANG TAEJU

656
00:58:42,686 --> 00:58:47,606
THE HUSBAND

657
00:59:28,148 --> 00:59:30,650
I wanted to check the applications
and selection records…

658
00:59:31,526 --> 00:59:33,069
Is it related to my dad?

659
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:36,405
About the phone
that Ha Jeongsoo had on him…

660
00:59:36,406 --> 00:59:39,325
It's the same number
that contacted Kim Gyeongae.

661
00:59:39,326 --> 00:59:41,827
I'll stay on Ms. Kim Gyeongae's case.

662
00:59:41,828 --> 00:59:46,207
Both my husband and I
were just pawns in this game.

663
00:59:46,208 --> 00:59:49,960
If someone actually tried
to have you killed through Dr. Ha…

664
00:59:49,961 --> 00:59:52,172
Do you think that person
will leave you alone now?

665
00:59:52,714 --> 00:59:55,299
If someone ever finds out,
I'll be in huge trouble.

666
00:59:55,300 --> 00:59:56,301
Today.

667
00:59:56,968 --> 00:59:58,303
It'll be over today.

668
00:59:59,638 --> 01:00:01,640
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon
